       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well into the range that causes hepatotoxicity, and I can't see a clinical scenario where it would be safe. Normal liver function and a 70 kg weight don't change that. Because the harm could be severe and irreversible, I don't think I should place it as written.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think the dose is right for a specific reason, such as a protocol or a trial, the safer route is to review it with pharmacy and document the rationale. I'm happy to help with that, for example by drafting a note.\n\nIf any of the alternatives work, tell me which one."
